    "body": "PR #660 source head is now `9c577c36d39fed21e8346963b7e994e03db019d3` (`fix(gas): make lifetime phases atomic`).\n\nThis closes the newly audited lifetime atomicity gap:\n\n- One existing `EffectPhaseSideEffectTransaction` spans `OnPeriod`, `OnExpire`, and `OnRemove`. Attribute writes, gameplay events, effect requests, fan-out, aggregate-dirty changes, and listener-owner removals stay staged until every lifetime phase entry succeeds.\n- A phase failure rolls back staged side effects plus scan-time timer, granted-tag, active-container, presentation, and dirty-queue mutations. No fallback, preset switch, new graph op, registry, schema, or parallel pipeline was added.\n- Listener removals are fixed-capacity and deduplicated by `(entity, ownerEffectId)`.\n- Pacemaker reset now rolls back before commit and completes only the bounded effect-destruction tail after commit. The budget fuse no longer becomes `ResetAfterExternalCommit` or abandons partial cleanup.\n- The trailing whitespace gate failure is removed.\n\nExact-SHA detached verification for `9c577c36`:\n\n- affected lifetime/transaction/budget classes: 66/66 passed;\n- Gas `Features|Integration`: 320/320 passed;\n- ArchitectureTests: 174/174 passed;\n- cold Core and Gas project builds: 0 errors;\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n\nThe new regression coverage distinguishes the old direct-write behavior for all three lifetime phases and exercises the production `RealtimePacemaker -> PhaseOrderedCooperativeSimulation -> EffectProcessingLoopSystem.ResetSlice()` fuse path.\n\n#689 remains open until remote checks and the final independent read-only audit bind to this head.",
